sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — MorphoEval overall 87.3/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Side-by-side generative reproduction and 1D space-time kymograph analysis of Wolfram (1984, 2002) Rule 30 cellular automata and Meinhardt & Klingler's (1987) activator-substrate-hormone reaction-diffusion PDE mapped onto a 3D Raup (1966) Conus textile shell mesh. Validated against OEIS A051023 (128/128 bits), Erica Jen's (1990) left-bijective inverse and diagonal period-doubling theorem (0 bit errors; dislocations at k = 0, 3, 8, 29, 400), and segmented OSU Conus textile specimen photography (H/W error 0.07%, 2D silhouette IoU 0.8353, white-tent chord CV 0.7069 vs specimen 0.6403). Overall 87.3/100 (faithfulness 86.4, reproducibility 89.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit fb234bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 89, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 85, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 89, Reproducibility package 89. Output judged: conus_textile_rule30_comparison.png: rendered output of 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py at fb234bc, image/png, 611089 B, 2640×1632 px, artifact_sha256 b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41 (sha256 b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41), spec_fingerprint 6baf9ffa515c0c89775df3b58f398571f7894e64d20534778dff610ad08bc313. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6baf9ffa515c0c89775df3b58f398571f7894e64d20534778dff610ad08bc313; artifact_sha256: b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/conus/conus_textile_reference.json=dfcb500d87a39390...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Wolfram (1983, 1984, 2002) introduces elementary cellular automaton Rule 30 (a_{t+1,i} = a_{t,i-1} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1})) as a discrete generative model of Conus textile tent pigmentation and poses the 2019 Rule 30 Prize Problems on the center column a_{t,0} (OEIS A051023) | Jen (1990) proves left-bijective spatial invertibility a_{t,i-1} = a_{t+1,i} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1}) and the left-cone diagonal period-doubling cascade d_k(t+1) = d_{k-2}(t) XOR (d_{k-1}(t) OR d_k(t)) gated by all-zero synchronizing barriers d_{k-1} = 0 | Meinhardt & Klingler (1987) formulate a 1D mantle-edge activator-substrate-hormone reaction-diffusion PDE generating self-extinguishing pigment triangles and V-shaped lesion recovery wakes; reconstructed_in_script: Exact Boolean and GF(2) ANF Rule 30 evolution, 1024-step single-seed light-cone, Jen (1990) left-bijective reconstruction and k=0..414 diagonal period-doubling cascade (k = 0, 3, 8, 29, 400), directional Boolean damage-cone ensemble, Meinhardt-Klingler PDE kymograph and lesion scar simulation, and 3D Raup Conus shell projection validated against segmented OSU Conus textile photography; transfer_boundary: Cross-model 1D space-time defect-front kymograph comparison linking Rule 30 / Meinhardt mantle wakes to Zhang-Goldstein-Levin (2025) frozen-defect cell sorting and Cervera-Levin-Mafe (2021) bioelectric domain-wall propagation; does_not_claim: Infinite-horizon proof of the open 2019 Wolfram Rule 30 Prize Problems #1-#3 (verifies finite-horizon statistics through t = 1024 and exact diagonal periods through k = 414)." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30> ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Extend 3D Conus shell texture comparison from 2D orthographic silhouette IoU to unwrapped cylindrical UV registration against 360-degree photogrammetry of a single Conus textile shell.",
            "remediation needed: Include the 4-variable Meinhardt (1995) branched-travelling-wave system with explicit point-arrest hormone pulses for large triangular tent cascades." ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.873"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30> rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation faithfully reproduces Conus textile Linnaeus, 1758 (textile cone snail) morphology" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon" .
}

